\v 35 \wj Say not ye, There are yet four months, and then cometh harvest? behold, I say unto you, Lift up your eyes, and look on the fields; for they are white already to harvest.\wj* 
\v 36 \wj And he that reapeth receiveth wages, and gathereth fruit unto life eternal: that both he that soweth and he that reapeth may rejoice together.\wj* 
\v 37 \wj And herein is that saying true, One soweth, and another reapeth.\wj* 
\v 38 \wj I sent you to reap that whereon ye bestowed no labour: other men laboured, and ye are entered into their labours.\wj* 
